body: "## Static compatibility regression after #156\n\nReviewed default commit `4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58` (package version `2026.10.25`), tree-identical to final PR head `73c3c77ace073535cba5f4725504570bed98e416`. This is source/artifact evidence, **not an executed old-host reproduction or a claim about npm publication of this merge**.\n\n### Expected / actual\nThe canonical compatibility work [#59](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/pull/59) and [pm-starter-zhwv](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58/.agents/pm/issues/pm-starter-zhwv.toon) establishes separate npm peer and host-enforced minimums. Both should admit hosts that can provide the required capability.\n\nBoth declarations still admit `2026.8.15`:\n- [manifest.json:7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58/manifest.json#L7): `pm_min_version: \"2026.8.15\"`.\n- [package.json](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58/package.json): peer `@unbrained/pm-cli >=2026.8.15`.\n\nBut [index.ts:237–249](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58/index.ts#L237-L249) now requires `ctx.sdk.client.listAllComplete`; demo and exporter share this reader. [README complete SDK reads](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-starter/blob/4f39fb2e9d207ad47297102bb56a1863568e6e58/README.md#complete-sdk-reads) documents a newer host requirement and explicit older-host failure. Documentation does not change either machine-enforced minimum.\n\n### Official floor artifact inspection\nDownloaded, **without executing package code or lifecycle scripts**:\n```sh\nnpm pack @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.15 --ignore-scripts\ntar -xzf unbrained-pm-cli-2026.8.15.tgz\ngrep -R -n 'listAllComplete' package\n```\nThe last search returns no matches. The artifact's `dist/sdk/runtime.js` defines `PmClient.list` but not `listAllComplete`. Its `CommandHandlerContext` does already expose optional `sdk`, so the precise missing floor capability is **the client method**, not a proven absence of all SDK injection. Tarball SHA-256: `ca30e51c298d2020cc4ac1cc0108e24bf3803ccb1b20667f3a1e1c6cde350b98`.\n\nConsequently an admitted floor host does not implement the newly unconditional call. The catch reports a failed read rather than false success, but consumers discover incompatibility at command/export time instead of installation/activation. Copied starter scaffolds inherit this stale compatibility promise.\n\n### Validation and limits\nOn Node `v24.22.1` with the unchanged locked development SDK `2026.10.20`, fresh isolated `npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `node --test test/sdk-adoption.test.ts` pass (4 tests). `node --test test/commands.test.ts test/compatibility-floor.test.ts` passes 87 tests. These validate the current development host, **not** the declared floor. The existing compatibility test checks agreement/order of declarations, not capability availability at that floor. No old-host execution, live provider calls, source edits, dependency changes, or releases were performed.\n\nAll-status issues/PRs and the canonical tracker were checked. #59 fixed the earlier absent-field problem; this is a new required-capability regression introduced by #156, not a request to reopen its merged PR.\n\n### Acceptance / regression criteria\n- Establish the earliest host that supports the complete-read and verified-history contracts actually used; align peer and `pm_min_version` declarations with that tested minimum, **or** preserve the old floor through a capability-preserving, SDK-owned compatibility path.\n- Do not restore ad hoc completeness parsing or weaken corruption refusal just to keep the old number.\n- Exercise demo and exporter on the declared minimum, including full bodies, terminal items, failed/incomplete reads and invalid-history refusal.\n- Verify below-minimum hosts are refused by the appropriate install/activation path; keep a regression that catches declarations lagging required SDK capabilities.\n- Preserve existing development pins unless separately justified; current-host green tests alone must not certify floor compatibility."
